# Licensing

This repository carries **three** different licences. Which one applies depends
on where a file lives:

| Path | Licence | Where |
|---|---|---|
| `tools/`, `scripts/` — pipeline & tooling | **MIT** | below |
| `server/` — Ritstjóri editorial server (incl. `greynir-sidecar/`) | **AGPL-3.0** | [`server/LICENSE`](server/LICENSE) |
| `books/` — translated content | **per-book Creative Commons** | below |

Repository-root configuration files (`package.json`, `eslint.config.js`,
`vitest.*`, `.gitignore` and similar) are offered under the MIT terms below.

## Pipeline and Tooling (MIT License)

The MIT grant covers the CNXML extraction, machine-translation integration,
reinjection and HTML-rendering pipeline: the `tools/` and `scripts/` directories
and the root configuration files listed above.

**It does not cover `server/`** (which is AGPL-3.0 — see `server/LICENSE`) **or
`books/`** (which is content under per-book Creative Commons terms — see below).

> Note for downstream users taking only `tools/` (and `scripts/`) under MIT —
> parts of that tooling reach into `server/`, which is AGPL-3.0. This changes
> nobody's rights either way; it is a combination caveat, recorded so that
> anyone taking the MIT tooling on its own knows what it expects to find beside
> it. The edges fall into four classes:
>
> 1. **Optional, guarded** — loads AGPL code inside a try/catch; the tool works
>    without `server/`.
>    - `tools/api-translate.js:1051` → `server/services/pipelineStatusService.js`
>
>    It warns and continues if the module is absent: translation runs correctly
>    without `server/`, and only a convenience status update is skipped.
> 2. **Required, unguarded** — loads AGPL code; the tool cannot load without
>    `server/`.
>    - `tools/validate-chapter.js:33` → `server/lib/chapterLabel`
>    - `scripts/validate-status.js:14` → `server/lib/chapterLabel.js`
>    - `scripts/backfill-mt-locks.js:99` → `server/lib/dbPath.js`
>    - `scripts/backfill-mt-locks.js:173` → `server/services/segmentParser.js`
>      (for `chapterDir`, which `segmentParser` re-exports at `:463`)
>    - `scripts/backfill-appendix-sections.js:198` → `server/lib/dbPath.js`
>    - `scripts/backfill-appendix-sections.js:201` →
>      `server/services/bookRegistration.js`
>    - `tools/generate-book-data.cjs:20` → `server/services/bookDataGenerator`
>    - `scripts/export-segment-edits.js` → `server/lib/chapterLabel.js`,
>      `server/services/segmentParser.js`, `server/lib/dbPath.js`
>    - `scripts/reattach-segment-edits.js` → `server/lib/chapterLabel.js`,
>      `server/services/segmentParser.js`,
>      `server/services/segmentEditorService.js`
>
>    The `chapterLabel` imports are deliberate: it is the project's canonical
>    converter between the two on-disk spellings of the appendices chapter, and
>    the repository's own rules require that conversion to happen only through
>    that module, never reimplemented inline. Taking `tools/` alone therefore
>    needs `server/lib/chapterLabel.js` (or an equivalent) alongside it.
> 3. **Data path, not code** — resolves a path under `server/` to read JSON;
>    loads no AGPL code.
>    - `tools/validate-pipeline-consistency.js:27` → `server/data`
>    - `tools/openstax-fetch.cjs:70` → `server/data/chemistry-2e.json`
>    - `tools/check-source-updates.js:134` → `server/data/${book}.json`
>    - `tools/translate-chapter-titles.js:46` → `server/data`
>    - `tools/generate-index.js:146` → `server/data`
> 4. **Package resolution, not code** — resolves a third-party package through
>    `server/node_modules`; loads no AGPL code. The package in every case is
>    `better-sqlite3`, which is itself MIT; it lives under `server/` because the
>    repository root has no dependency on it.
>    - `tools/lib/safeWrite.js:50` and `scripts/backfill-mt-locks.js:98` anchor
>      a `createRequire` inside `server/`, then load the bare specifier.
>    - `scripts/export-segment-edits.js:55` and
>      `scripts/backfill-appendix-sections.js:199` join the
>      `server/node_modules/better-sqlite3` path directly.
>    - `tools/merge-glossary.js:495` tries that path and falls back to the bare
>      specifier.
>
> This list is the authoritative enumeration — update it here when an edge is
> added or removed, and re-derive rather than trusting it, searching for both a
> literal `'../server/…'` and a computed `path.join(…, 'server', …)`.

